	quest.120240EC8E0079E4.title: "Evolve a Pokemon!"
	quest.1C0418F172DF6BDE.quest_desc: ["Now that you have all the basics down, It's time to prove that you're the very best, like no one ever was!"]
	quest.1C0418F172DF6BDE.quest_subtitle: "Win a Pokemon Battle!"
	quest.1C0418F172DF6BDE.title: "Fight!"
	quest.2C8BA75EF1C9F231.quest_desc: ["Use your newly crafted Pokeballs to catch a new team member!"]
	quest.2C8BA75EF1C9F231.quest_subtitle: "Make a New Friend!"
	quest.2C8BA75EF1C9F231.title: "Catch a Pokemon"
	quest.2DFFE5EA93E566E3.quest_desc: ["By combining a regular fishing rod with a Poke Rod Upgrade Template and your choice of Pokeball in a smithing table, you get a Poke Rod! This Tool allows you to fish for Pokemon in bodies of water. You can attach different berries to the rod as bait to influence what you can find!"]
	quest.2DFFE5EA93E566E3.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Poke Rod"
	quest.2DFFE5EA93E566E3.title: "Let's Go Fishing!"
	quest.2ED92A41A84E9064.quest_desc: ["Do it. I &oDare You"]
	quest.2ED92A41A84E9064.quest_subtitle: "Release a Shiny Pokemon"
	quest.2ED92A41A84E9064.title: "How Shiny is it Really?"
	quest.31B52A057D58F766.quest_desc: ["Level up a Pokemon to level 100, the highest possible level"]
	quest.31B52A057D58F766.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Max Level Pokemon"
	quest.31B52A057D58F766.title: "LEVEL 9000!"
	quest.33E92C3B3665EA7B.quest_desc: ["You can also heal your Pokemon using various healing items, that can be crafted using these base ingredients."]
	quest.33E92C3B3665EA7B.quest_subtitle: "Obtain Useful Ingredients Used for Crafting Healing Items "
	quest.33E92C3B3665EA7B.title: "Who needs Doctors?"
	quest.358F86E457ECED59.quest_subtitle: "Do it"
	quest.358F86E457ECED59.title: "The Best Fisherman!"
	quest.36459C1C9E06DAFC.quest_desc: ["Tier 3 Pokeballs make up some of the best available balls in the game, giving you (almost) the best chances of catching a Pokemon!"]
	quest.36459C1C9E06DAFC.quest_subtitle: "Make a Tier 3 Pokeball!"
	quest.36459C1C9E06DAFC.title: "Even Better Pokeballs?!"
	quest.3750550195B5E57D.quest_desc: ["Pokeballs come in all sorts of variations that can increase the chance of catching a Pokemon in different situations"]
	quest.3750550195B5E57D.quest_subtitle: "Make a Tier 2 Pokeball!"
	quest.3750550195B5E57D.title: "Better Pokeballs?"
	quest.4C3ED55BD0ABCCCB.quest_desc: ["Fossils can be found in suspicious sand and gravel found in various structures around the world. When placed in the Fossil Analyser that you crafted before, along with a Resoration Tank full of biological matter, it will begin the revival process."]
	quest.4C3ED55BD0ABCCCB.quest_subtitle: "Revive a Fossil Pokemon!"
	quest.4C3ED55BD0ABCCCB.title: "Jurassic Park"
	quest.579A062E193ED1E4.quest_subtitle: "Ethers and Elixers restore the PP (power points) of your Pokemon's moves!"
	quest.579A062E193ED1E4.title: "Elixirs"
	quest.62AA0AD78E3DEF2D.quest_desc: ["Basic Pokeballs can be crafted using apricorns and copper ingots. These will enable you to catch more Pokemon!"]
	quest.62AA0AD78E3DEF2D.quest_subtitle: "Craft Your First Pokeball!"
	quest.62AA0AD78E3DEF2D.title: "Pokeballs"
	quest.63450C3E4316EA6C.quest_desc: ["As you battle and collect more Pokemon, you'll find that you want to use different pokemon, or that your team members get injured. This is where the Healing Machine and PC come in! The Healing Machine will allow you to heal your party, and the PC will allow you to move your Pokemon around!"]
	quest.63450C3E4316EA6C.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Healing Machine and a PC"
	quest.63450C3E4316EA6C.title: "Machines!"
	quest.68D9E7932F6FF350.quest_desc: ["When these three machines are placed together, they become capable of reviving fossil Pokemon!"]
	quest.68D9E7932F6FF350.quest_subtitle: "Obtain the Machines Needed to Revive Fossils"
	quest.68D9E7932F6FF350.title: "More Machines!"
	quest.6B2E752C5AFDF0A1.quest_desc: ["Catching lots of Pokemon can take up precious space in your PC, so its always handy to release the ones you don't want! Releasing a Pokemon also has a chance of dropping a Type Gem of the same type of the Pokemon that you released!"]
	quest.6B2E752C5AFDF0A1.quest_subtitle: "Release a Pokemon!"
	quest.6B2E752C5AFDF0A1.title: "No Thank You."
	quest.6BD38D2C7D3B2E20.quest_desc: ["Having a full party greatly increases your chances of winning any battle!"]
	quest.6BD38D2C7D3B2E20.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Full Party of 6 Pokemon!"
	quest.6BD38D2C7D3B2E20.title: "A Full Party!"
	quest.6DD7C24A3310F912.quest_subtitle: "Revives bring your Pokemon back from fainting!"
	quest.6DD7C24A3310F912.title: "Revives"
	quest.70A838F4A55AB8BE.quest_desc: ["The Pokedex is used to keep record of all the Pokemon you see and requires apricorns to craft. There are over 1000 Pokemon to date, how many can you catch?"]
	quest.70A838F4A55AB8BE.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Pokedex!"
	quest.70A838F4A55AB8BE.title: "Gotta Catch 'em all!"
	quest.797E07C6D1488B44.quest_desc: ["Sometimes you'll obtain a Pokemon that you dont want, that another person does! Trading can also cause certain Pokemon to evolve, however using a Link Cable also has the same effect."]
	quest.797E07C6D1488B44.quest_subtitle: "Trade a Pokemon With Another Player, or Obtain a Link Cable"
	quest.797E07C6D1488B44.title: "I Will Remember You..."
